      "urls": [
        {
          "description": "This page provides general information and certain policies for the .Apple Top-Level Domain (TLD). A TLD is the highest level of a domain name (like ‘.com’ in the apple.com domain name) and generally represents the purpose of the domain name (like how ‘.com’ generally is used for ‘commercial’ websites). Apple was authorized by ICANN, the global regulator of Internet domain names, to be the registry operator for the .Apple TLD. As the registry operator, Apple will manage and set certain policies for the",
